+To-Do v1.22.11 Self Test
+=========================
+Base: v1.22.10 NoteDarkElectricLinks
+Target: v1.22.11
+
+Feature acceptance model
+- Adding a file does NOT create/show an annotation.
+- Three-dot action sheet has a small top-right +附注 / 编辑附注 action.
+- Annotation is title-less and visually attached below its file.
+- One file has at most one annotation.
+- Annotation stays inside the existing Note editor host; no second/nested editor focus owner.
+- Empty annotation disappears when the user taps elsewhere and is pruned on next open.
+- Deleting an attachment also removes its annotation.
+- Annotation text remains searchable and uses the existing autosave / B-S-H / link pipeline.
+
+Static checks PASS
+- Node JS syntax.
+- ui/todo.html == Android asset mirror.
+- inline main script == script_0.js.
+- Static DOM IDs unique; noteFileAnnotationAction unique.
+- Android XML parse.
+- versionCode=44 / versionName=1.22.11 / package unchanged.
+- MainActivity / NoteFileViewerActivity / ImportReceiverActivity / Manifest / FileProvider byte-identical to V1.22.10.
+- Reminder/Daily/Banner/Snooze locked core 20/20 SHA-256 exact.
+- Existing business localStorage key literals unchanged.
+- 20 high-risk editor/link/image functions exact vs V1.22.10.
+- createNoteFileCard and insertPickedFileItems exact vs V1.22.10.
+- Existing WeChat / QQ / More Apps / Delete Attachment action grid exact vs V1.22.10.
+- insertImageMarkerAtCaret / insertFileMarkerAtCaret differ only by the annotation-only block-placement guard.
+
+Headless Chromium micro-tests PASS
+- Multi-card stack A/B/C -> add annotation to B: card B is isolated, one annotation is created, A/B/C card nodes preserved.
+- Cancel an empty annotation: split stacks merge back to one stack when no other annotation blocks the merge.
+- Removing annotation A while file B still owns annotation B does NOT merge B into the wrong visual group.
+- Root-level Enter inside annotation produces <br> inside the SAME annotation rather than cloning the annotation block.
+- Enter inside UL/LI keeps native Chromium list behavior and creates a new LI inside the same annotation.
+
+Target-phone checks
+1. Add a file: UI must remain exactly the same until three-dot > +附注 is chosen.
+2. +附注: action sheet closes, a small inset paper-note appears below the selected file, keyboard opens at its caret.
+3. Type multiple lines with Enter; there must still be exactly one annotation block.
+4. Tap B/S/H/list/link typing in the annotation; existing toolbar/keyboard must behave as normal Note text.
+5. Empty the annotation and tap elsewhere: annotation disappears without leaving blank space.
+6. Reopen three-dot with an existing annotation: top-right reads 编辑附注 and focuses the existing text.
+7. Delete file: both file and its annotation disappear; physical file deletion behavior remains unchanged.
+8. Import several files at once: display stays unchanged; only explicitly annotated card gets isolated.
+9. While caret is in annotation, choose Add Image/Add File: new block lands after annotation, not inside it.
+10. Regression: long-note IME toolbar stays above keyboard, low caret reveals, no jump-to-top.
+11. Regression: B/S/H manual typing states, HTTP(S) links, image/PDF pinch zoom, image focus-safe preview.
+12. Regression: Reminder/Daily/Banner/Snooze.
+
+Gradle
+- An offline Gradle wrapper build is attempted separately. If the wrapper distribution is not cached, this environment cannot produce a compiler result; Android Studio/Windows remains the final build verification.
